It is no longer entangled.

36:05.200 --> 36:09.380
It could be perfectly described as a classical, local mixture of states.

36:09.380 --> 36:11.280
Consider my mind officially blown.

36:11.840 --> 36:19.700
Are you saying that entanglement, the thing that Einstein hated, the thing that quantum computers rely on, might just be an artifact of using the wrong math?

36:20.180 --> 36:27.200
Like if I put on real number goggles, two particles look deeply, fundamentally entangled across space.

36:27.540 --> 36:36.620
But if I take those off and swap them for complex number goggles, those exact same particles just look like two completely normal, classically correlated objects.

36:36.620 --> 36:40.660
That is exactly what the math demonstrates for this specific family of states.

36:40.980 --> 36:43.000
Now, we ought to be very careful not to overstate this.

36:43.100 --> 36:47.300
The manuscript is not claiming that all entanglement in our universe is an illusion.

36:48.180 --> 36:55.720
Standard complex quantum mechanics has plenty of states, like the famous bell states, that are genuinely entangled even when you use complex numbers.

36:55.920 --> 36:57.540
Right. I mean, quantum computers still work.

36:57.880 --> 36:58.400
Exactly.

36:58.400 --> 37:06.000
What this proves is how deeply the concept of entanglement is tethered to the mathematical field you are using to describe the local systems.

37:06.620 --> 37:13.580
Entanglement is not always an intrinsic, objective property of a physical state matrix floating out in the ether.

37:14.120 --> 37:17.680
It is a property of the state relative to the rules of your theory.

37:17.860 --> 37:18.580
That makes sense.

37:18.940 --> 37:26.840
If your theory doesn't have enough local parameters, like the real numbers, the math will essentially invent entanglement to hide the extra information.

37:26.840 --> 37:30.180
This is an incredible structural insight.

37:30.400 --> 37:39.320
We have built this towering mathematical architecture, found these wild, hidden cryptographic variables, and watched entanglement shift based on our goggles.

37:39.740 --> 37:42.200
And we haven't even assumed standard quantum mechanics yet.

37:42.260 --> 37:43.740
We just follow the rules of probability.

37:44.200 --> 37:47.640
But now, in section six, we have to cash in our chips.

37:47.640 --> 37:51.540
Yes. This brings us to part three of the book, The Recovered Structure.

37:51.780 --> 38:00.120
It's time to see what it actually costs to derive the textbook formulas that physicists use every day, because Flyxion is incredibly rigorous about auditing assumptions.

38:00.700 --> 38:05.680
It is so easy in theoretical physics to accidentally smuggle in the answer you want without realizing it.

38:05.880 --> 38:08.960
It's the most common trap in foundational physics, actually.

38:09.460 --> 38:14.020
You try to derive quantum mechanics, but you accidentally assume half of it on page one.

38:14.020 --> 38:18.400
Chapter 18 of this manuscript is dedicated to the Assumption Audit.

38:18.940 --> 38:30.280
It literally collects every single explicitly flagged assumption required to get from our bare classical probability simplex to a modern graduate-level physics textbook.

38:30.760 --> 38:32.780
And the shocking part is that there are only four of them.

38:33.200 --> 38:35.700
Four basic costs to earn the entire textbook.

38:36.260 --> 38:40.660
Let's walk the listener through these, one by one, because this is where the magic trick is revealed.

38:41.080 --> 38:43.580
Assumption one, we have already spent a lot of time on.

38:44.020 --> 38:45.040
Local tomography.

38:45.820 --> 38:49.700
The assumption that a joint state is perfectly described by local tests.

38:50.320 --> 38:54.960
We saw that if you demand this principle, it brutally filters out the real numbers and the quaternions,

38:55.220 --> 38:59.700
and selects complex numbers as the unique Goldilocks fit for our state spaces.

39:00.060 --> 39:03.380
Okay, one assumption down, and we have complex vector spaces.

39:03.560 --> 39:04.480
What is Assumption two?

39:04.680 --> 39:09.500
Assumption two is that pure states are operationally representable as frame-completable vectors.

39:09.500 --> 39:11.620
Uh, that sounds horribly dense.

39:11.700 --> 39:12.700
Can you break that down for me?

39:12.920 --> 39:14.340
It's operationally very simple.

39:14.980 --> 39:20.760
In part one, we talked about contexts or frames, which are just entire sets of mutually exclusive outcomes,

39:21.020 --> 39:24.960
like the six faces of a die or a full orthogonal basis in linear algebra.

39:25.180 --> 39:25.300
Right.

39:25.300 --> 39:31.340
Assumption two just says that if you prepare a single, absolutely pure state of certainty in your lab,

39:31.480 --> 39:36.760
we can mathematically treat it as one specific arrow, one vector belonging to one of those full frames.

39:36.920 --> 39:39.260
Okay, so a state is just an arrow in a framework.

39:39.500 --> 39:40.480
Why is that powerful?

39:40.480 --> 39:47.840
Because once you allow that simple geometric mapping, the famous Born rule literally falls out of the math for free.

39:48.200 --> 39:54.440
The Born rule being the rule that says probability is the amplitude squared, the thing Max Born won a Nobel Prize for.

39:54.600 --> 39:55.760
That exact rule.

39:56.340 --> 39:58.760
In most textbooks, the Born rule is a postulate.

39:59.080 --> 40:00.600
It's just handed down from on high.

40:00.840 --> 40:02.340
That should square the amplitude.

40:02.620 --> 40:02.820
Yeah.

40:02.940 --> 40:08.560
But Flyxion shows that if states are frame-completable vectors, the Born rule is mathematically inevitable.

40:08.560 --> 40:17.960
It is mathematically identical to extracting a single column from the un-stochastic transition matrices we proved must exist back in section two.

40:18.580 --> 40:20.480
You don't have to postulate the Born rule.

40:20.920 --> 40:24.400
It is a structural consequence of classical probability limits.

40:24.540 --> 40:25.460
That is incredible.

40:26.000 --> 40:27.020
Okay, assumption three.

40:28.180 --> 40:30.620
Measurement outcomes are labeled by real numbers.

40:31.340 --> 40:34.680
This is largely a modeling choice about how human beings do science.

40:34.680 --> 40:42.460
When we measure something in a lab, the position of a particle, its momentum, its spin, we don't read imaginary numbers off the digital screen.

40:42.600 --> 40:46.340
The screen prints out a real number, five meters per second or plus one half spin.

40:46.480 --> 40:46.640
Right.

40:46.760 --> 40:48.940
Our rulers are made of real numbers.

40:49.080 --> 40:56.380
If you formally assume that outcomes must be real numbers, and you combine that with the sharp projective geometry of the probability frames we just built,

40:56.740 --> 41:00.460
you mathematically force all quantum observables to be Hermitian operators.

41:00.600 --> 41:01.820
Another piece of heavy jargon.

41:01.820 --> 41:06.500
A Hermitian operator is just a matrix that has entirely real Eakin values.

41:06.860 --> 41:09.620
It's the standard tool for observables in quantum math.

41:10.360 --> 41:13.640
Again, textbooks postulate that observables are Hermitian.

41:14.160 --> 41:19.460
This manuscript proves that if your ruler reads real numbers, the operator must be Hermitian.

41:20.200 --> 41:21.880
It's an inevitable equivalence.

41:22.240 --> 41:24.400
Which brings us to the final piece of the puzzle.

41:25.020 --> 41:25.780
Assumption four.

41:25.780 --> 41:30.060
Up until now, everything we've talked about has been a static snapshot.

41:30.640 --> 41:31.740
An arrow in a frame.

41:32.160 --> 41:33.240
But the universe moves.

41:34.120 --> 41:38.280
Assumption four is that time evolution is a strongly continuous unitary group.

41:38.280 --> 41:45.220
Let's spend some deep time unpacking that phrase, because I know what it leads to, and I want the listener to really feel the weight of it.

41:45.260 --> 41:46.600
Let's break it down word by word.

41:46.860 --> 41:47.840
Unitary, we already know.

41:48.320 --> 41:51.580
It means the transformation is perfectly balanced like our bistochastic matrices.

41:52.220 --> 41:53.420
Information is never lost.

41:53.540 --> 41:55.920
The probabilities always balance out to 100%.

41:55.920 --> 41:56.220
Okay.

41:56.220 --> 41:58.720
Continuous means time flows smoothly.

41:59.280 --> 42:02.620
It doesn't jump in glitchy, discrete frames like a lagging video game.

42:02.800 --> 42:05.500
It evolves smoothly from one millisecond to the next.

42:05.820 --> 42:09.040
Okay, so time is smooth and information is preserved.

42:09.380 --> 42:12.620
That seems like the most basic definition of reality possible.

42:12.940 --> 42:13.380
It is.

42:13.780 --> 42:18.300
But if you formally assume those two properties, a continuous unitary group,

42:18.300 --> 42:22.320
you can apply a piece of pure mathematics called Stone's Theorem,

42:22.820 --> 42:26.700
which deals with the generators of linear, ordinary differential equations.

42:27.360 --> 42:33.180
If you run that theorem on our continuous unitary evolution, a specific differential equation drops out.

42:33.360 --> 42:36.120
And that equation is Schrodinger's equation.

42:36.400 --> 42:36.740
Yes.

42:37.140 --> 42:39.540
The most famous equation in quantum mechanics.

42:39.840 --> 42:42.580
The equation that governs the wave function of the universe.

42:42.720 --> 42:43.580
Let's just pause on that.

42:43.640 --> 42:45.160
You derive Schrodinger's equation.

42:45.160 --> 42:49.800
Like, you don't just write it on a chalkboard as Axiom 6 and tell the grad students to memorize it.

42:49.940 --> 42:50.280
Exactly.

42:50.700 --> 42:55.220
In this framework, Schrodinger's equation is just the infinitesimal mathematical consequence

42:55.220 --> 42:58.960
of assuming that probabilities evolve smoothly and reversibly.

42:59.400 --> 43:02.080
It is a mathematical theorem, not a physical postulate.

43:02.420 --> 43:05.480
It really is like reverse engineering a massive video game.

43:05.900 --> 43:08.540
Imagine we are trying to understand how a game engine works,

43:08.900 --> 43:12.620
but we don't have access to the source code, which is the textbook physics.

43:12.680 --> 43:13.580
We just have the game.

43:13.580 --> 43:18.020
So we poke around, we map out the hitboxes, we test how gravity behaves,

43:18.320 --> 43:20.800
we find the invisible walls at the edge of the map.

43:21.040 --> 43:22.820
Defining the admissibility constraints.

43:23.000 --> 43:23.200
Right.

43:23.500 --> 43:30.120
And from just four simple rules about those boundaries, local tomography, vectors, real rulers, smooth time,

43:30.520 --> 43:34.880
we perfectly reconstruct the entire million-line source code from scratch.

43:34.880 --> 43:37.700
It is a tour de force of foundational physics.

43:38.100 --> 43:43.640
It strips away a century of historical baggage and shows exactly what the quantum architecture actually rests on.

43:44.160 --> 43:48.280
And as a final flex, the book even derives Neymar's Dilation Theorem from scratch.

43:48.380 --> 43:49.420
What does that theorem do?

43:49.760 --> 43:51.580
It deals with messy reality.

43:52.120 --> 43:55.200
In a real lab, you rarely make perfect, sharp measurements.

43:55.540 --> 43:57.340
Your detectors have noise, they are fuzzy.

43:57.720 --> 44:00.140
These are called POVMs, generalized measurements.

44:00.140 --> 44:04.800
Neymar's Theorem proves that every messy, fuzzy measurement you can possibly make

44:04.800 --> 44:11.060
is mathematically identical to a sharp, perfect measurement happening on a larger system that includes the environment.

44:11.580 --> 44:15.020
We just trace out the environment, we ignore it, and the measurement looks fuzzy to us.

44:15.140 --> 44:16.300
So let's take stock.

44:16.740 --> 44:20.440
Four assumptions give us standard, complex-numbered quantum mechanics.

44:20.440 --> 44:24.000
We tried to use real numbers early on, and they broke on the three-way roundabout.

44:24.480 --> 44:26.260
They broke on the Escher staircase cycle.

44:26.520 --> 44:30.600
They failed the local tomography dimension counting by hiding cryptographic keys.

44:31.100 --> 44:35.620
Complex numbers swooped in, saved the day, and effortlessly generated the textbook formulas.

44:35.960 --> 44:38.560
So the book proved that the universe must be complex.

44:39.060 --> 44:39.780
Case closed, right?

44:40.160 --> 44:43.120
And here is where the 2026 plot twist drops.

44:43.740 --> 44:45.880
Because if you read the preface of the manuscript,

44:46.500 --> 44:49.980
Flyxion explicitly warns the reader against taking that exact conclusion.

44:50.540 --> 44:53.440
To say, this book proves the universe requires complex numbers,

44:53.860 --> 44:56.840
is to claim something the author explicitly argues against.

44:57.100 --> 44:58.120
Which blew my mind.

44:58.660 --> 45:00.180
Let's unpack this in section 7.

45:00.560 --> 45:01.400
The plot twist.

45:02.080 --> 45:04.180
Do we actually need complex numbers?

45:04.840 --> 45:08.700
If everything we just talked about for the last hour is mathematically true,

45:09.060 --> 45:12.360
how is there possibly a loophole left for real numbers?

45:12.360 --> 45:16.140
The loophole lies in the deepest, most invisible assumption of all.

45:17.260 --> 45:17.740
Representation.

45:17.740 --> 45:23.220
To understand it, the book introduces a concept coined by mathematician Tristan Needham

45:23.220 --> 45:25.020
called the amplitwist.

45:25.420 --> 45:25.940
amplitwist.

45:26.000 --> 45:26.920
I love that word.

45:27.020 --> 45:29.680
It perfectly describes what is actually happening.

45:30.540 --> 45:34.940
We have this mystical imaginary number e, the square root of negative 1.

45:35.340 --> 45:37.600
For a century, people have treated it like magic.

45:38.060 --> 45:42.260
But what does multiplying a number by e actually do geometrically?

45:42.260 --> 45:46.200
It rotates a vector by 90 degrees in the complex plane, a quarter turn.

45:46.280 --> 45:46.720
Exactly.

45:47.160 --> 45:48.980
Complex multiplication isn't mystical at all.

45:49.140 --> 45:52.440
It is literally just a combination of scaling the length of an arrow, the amplitude,

45:52.820 --> 45:55.520
and rotating the arrow, the twist, amplitwist.

45:55.900 --> 45:57.600
But here's the crucial realization.

45:58.100 --> 46:00.440
You don't need imaginary numbers to do a quarter turn.

46:00.480 --> 46:01.940
You can just do it with real geometry.

46:01.940 --> 46:02.620
Yes.

46:03.360 --> 46:09.200
You can write down a perfectly normal 2x2 matrix of completely real classical numbers

46:09.200 --> 46:13.240
that takes any vector in a 2D plane and rotates it by 90 degrees.

46:13.780 --> 46:18.000
Specifically, it's a matrix with a 0 and a negative 1 on the top row and a 1 and a 0

46:18.000 --> 46:18.940
on the bottom row.

46:19.020 --> 46:19.560
Wait a second.

46:19.800 --> 46:21.500
0, negative 1, 1, 0.

46:21.600 --> 46:24.620
Is that the anti-symmetric J matrix we talked about earlier?

46:24.620 --> 46:29.340
It is the exact same J matrix, the same matrix that caused all the trouble in our local tomography

46:29.340 --> 46:31.940
dimension counting, the quarter turn generator.

46:32.560 --> 46:36.040
It is literally the imaginary unit eiding in a real number disguise.

46:36.640 --> 46:40.560
Everything that e does in quantum mechanics can be written entirely using real matrices

46:40.560 --> 46:41.300
containing J.

46:41.300 --> 46:46.240
So the mystical imaginary E was basically just a physical quarter turn rotation hiding

46:46.240 --> 46:48.220
in a mathematical trench coat this whole time.

46:48.580 --> 46:48.820
Yes.

46:49.480 --> 46:51.540
And this brings us to the cutting edge of the field.

46:51.540 --> 46:56.020
The 2025 and 2026 literature discussed in Chapter 18.

46:56.760 --> 47:00.940
Papers by researchers like Hoffermann and Woods and Barrios-Hita and colleagues.

47:01.840 --> 47:05.060
These physicists asked a brilliant disruptive question.

47:06.020 --> 47:11.840
If I is just a real rotation matrix in disguise, can we do all of quantum mechanics using only

47:11.840 --> 47:12.580
real numbers?

47:12.880 --> 47:14.960
But we literally just proved you can't.

47:15.060 --> 47:20.380
We proved real numbers fail local tomography because of that hidden J tensor J dimension,

47:20.380 --> 47:22.040
the math didn't balance.

47:22.300 --> 47:25.860
Ah, but how do we combine Alice and Bob's systems when we counted the dimensions?

47:26.340 --> 47:28.420
We used the standard Kronecker tensor product.

47:28.560 --> 47:30.640
The standard way you multiply matrices together.

47:30.740 --> 47:30.960
Yes.

47:31.180 --> 47:33.480
That is the assumption we didn't even realize we were making.

47:33.880 --> 47:37.940
We assumed that the mathematical rule for how systems compose was fixed and unquestionable.

47:38.060 --> 47:38.900
Oh my god.

47:38.900 --> 47:43.900
These new 2025 and 2026 papers show that you can do quantum mechanics using entirely real

47:43.900 --> 47:48.480
numbers, reproducing every single experimental prediction of standard quantum mechanics, from

47:48.480 --> 47:53.360
entanglement to Schrodinger's equation, if you change the mathematical rule for how systems

47:53.360 --> 47:53.800
compose.

47:53.960 --> 47:54.840
You change the multiplication.

47:55.380 --> 47:55.780
Exactly.

47:56.360 --> 48:00.860
If you abandon the standard Kronecker product and use a different mathematical representation

48:00.860 --> 48:06.080
of the tensor product that naturally accommodates the J matrix structure, real numbers work

48:06.080 --> 48:06.580
perfectly.

48:07.140 --> 48:08.600
The missing dimensions vanish.

48:08.960 --> 48:10.160
The contradictions resolve.

48:10.740 --> 48:11.600
That is just.

48:11.720 --> 48:13.100
The irony is unbelievable.

48:13.340 --> 48:17.060
After ruling out real numbers in section two with the roundabout, and section three with

48:17.060 --> 48:21.620
the Escher stairs, and section four with the cryptographic key, we find out at the very

48:21.620 --> 48:28.020
end that real numbers can actually work if we just change our definition of the word and when we say Alice and Bob.

48:28.160 --> 48:30.300
It is the ultimate lesson in theoretical physics.

48:30.800 --> 48:33.840
It reveals a profound truth about reality versus representation.

48:33.840 --> 48:37.720
The apparent necessity of complex numbers wasn't a physical law.

48:38.060 --> 48:39.420
It was a representation hazard.

48:40.200 --> 48:43.540
The universe has a specific, hard-coded geometric structure.

48:44.160 --> 48:47.240
It fundamentally requires a quarter-turn rotation to function.

48:47.960 --> 48:49.500
That is the physical truth.

48:49.540 --> 48:51.480
And how we spell that truth is up to us.

48:51.860 --> 48:52.380
Precisely.

48:53.040 --> 48:56.880
We humans chose to write that rotation using the symbol I.

48:57.240 --> 48:59.400
We chose to use the Kronecker tensor product.

48:59.400 --> 49:04.680
And because we made those specific choices, we forced ourselves into a complex numbered framework.

49:05.300 --> 49:10.800
But if we change our mathematical conventions, real numbers can describe the exact same physical reality.

49:11.360 --> 49:14.640
The underlying physical truth is the geometry, the structure.

49:15.060 --> 49:17.040
It is not the alphabet we use to spell it out.

49:17.280 --> 49:20.400
It really makes you question everything you learned in physics class.

49:20.620 --> 49:23.400
And just to throw one more wrench into the gears before we finish,

