51:21.140 --> 51:24.660
It is a stunning display of what theoretical physics should be.

51:25.260 --> 51:28.420
Stripping away the dogma, showing exactly what our assumptions cost,

51:28.420 --> 51:31.620
and carefully separating the structural reality of the universe

51:31.620 --> 51:34.900
from the human conventions we use to write it down on a whiteboard.

51:35.320 --> 51:38.000
It forces us to distinguish the territory from the map.

51:38.100 --> 51:41.500
Which leaves me with a final thought for you, the listener, to mull over.

51:42.160 --> 51:46.020
If the absolute necessity of imaginary numbers and quantum mechanics,

51:46.260 --> 51:49.400
something that Nobel laureates have sworn by for a hundred years,

