That is the ultimate question for the next century of physics.

52:00.540 --> 52:03.020
When you look at the fundamental laws of reality,

52:03.220 --> 52:07.340
when you see a complex equation explaining the birth of a star or the spin of an electron,

52:07.960 --> 52:12.360
how much of what you are seeing is the true, raw, geometric universe,

52:12.740 --> 52:16.040
and how much is just the human mathematical lens you are looking through,

52:16.120 --> 52:19.560
something to chew on the next time you hear a physicist confidently declare

